text='# NOT_CERTIFIED — statistical power and guarantee audit\n\nThe target is the expected positive nDCG10 regret of the whole executed randomized policy relative to fixed exact FullVisual, including all routing randomization. It is not a guarantee on mean signed gap, per-query correctness, or merely the Rerank arm. Each loss is in [0,1]. epsilon=.05 and delta=.01 remain unchanged.\n\nCal81 contains81 candidate query families by frozen metadata, but lexical/embedding separation and nonoverlap do not prove independent identically sampled tasks. Original query-generation prompts, document sampling and conditional dependencies are not fully known. Shared documents are compatible with fixed-corpus query generalization only under explicit query sampling assumptions; 23 document components are not81 IID observations and cannot be silently substituted for n.\n\nFor an ideal single fixed policy with81 independent all-zero bounded losses, the exact Bernoulli extremal/Clopper–Pearson upper bound is 1-.01**(1/81)=0.0552679653, above .05. ln(1/alpha)/n is a convenient logarithmic reference, NOT the exact CP value. Minimum90 IID samples for epsilon.05 and112 for budget.040404 are optimistic all-zero single-policy lower bounds. Nonzero risk, multiple candidates, sparse harms and dependence require more, not fewer, data. Conservative randomized reference mixtures can in principle satisfy tighter policy risk; this calculation does not prove all nontrivial mixtures impossible.\n\nA distributional delta-PAC certificate needs a defensible independent sampling design (or a theorem matching the actual dependence). Fixed finite-public-benchmark heldout reporting is a separate descriptive target. No simple-random-sample-without-replacement design/proof for a fixed finite population has been established by this inherited split, so no finite-population certificate is issued. Cal/Eval labels AND plan scores were not accessed.\n\nPower grid lists all declared candidate counts and hypothetical budgets. No observed Cal losses are used. Additional500 independently sampled families is a planning target, not a proof of power or approved label budget. A 100-family variance/pipeline pilot remains independent from future evaluation and cannot be repeated to manufacture independent n.\n'
C.prose(C.R/'statistical_power_feasibility.md',text);C.prose(C.R/'independent_unit_report.md','# INSUFFICIENT independence evidence\n\n'+json.dumps(C.clean({'Cal_query_n':81,'effective_IID_n':'UNKNOWN','existing_assumptions':assumptions}),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n\nDo not use label-free deduplication as an independence theorem. The IID contract, future unit sampling and human labeling budget remain pending user decision.\n')
C.prose(C.R/'release_gate.md','# BLOCKED_CAL_EVAL_RELEASE / NOT_CERTIFIED\n\nRequired before any future Cal release: justified contract and independent/effective units; frozen candidate order, estimator and alpha list; immutable model/index/code/data hash lock; power audit; user separately authorizes Cal. Eval separately requires all methods frozen and explicit authorization. None of these steps is waived by this report. Current stage performs zero Cal/Eval qrels or score reads.\n')
